  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# New Features\n      - Added `Grid.OnKeyDown` event. Handle Enter / Escape / Ctrl+S etc. from script. IME composition keys are filtered automatically.\n      - Added `Field.HasFocus()` script method to detect focus state.\n      - Added `OnValidateInput` script event on every Field. Customize Submit-time validation per field. AutoSubmit also runs validation now.\n      - Added `Module.IsValid` and `ListField.IsValid` properties.\n      - `Task` and `KeyboardEventArgs` are now usable from script (e.g. `Task.Delay(1)`).\n      - Dialogs / Popups / Panels now re-render when the hosted Module's state changes (so `Module.ClassName` etc. reflects properly).\n\n      # Fixes\n      - `IdField` `AllowEmptySearch` option now works (previously the empty/non-empty options were not shown).\n      - `SelectField` / `RadioGroupField`: Japanese display name for `AllowOrSearch` changed from \"直接入力または選択\" to \"OR検索を許可\" to match the actual behavior.\n      - `ListField` / `DetailListField` / `TileListField`: search UI dropdown width now follows column settings (Stretch by default).\n      - `ListField` loading now reuses a single internal context object across rows.\n\n      # Breaking Changes\n      - `OnDataChanged` event order changed: the field's own `OnDataChanged` script now runs BEFORE upper-level notifications (Layout `OnFieldDataChanged`, parent's `OnChildDataChanged`, UI re-render). Code that relied on reading auto-derived values (e.g. composite IDs) inside the source field's `OnDataChanged` will see the OLD derived value; move that logic into the IdField's own `OnDataChanged`.",
